es/7/labels","id":173770,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMTczNzcw","number":7,"title":"GLM 0.9.9","description":"","creator":{"login":"Groovounet","id":367227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzIyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":2,"closed_issues":212,"state":"open","created_at":"2012-09-12T10:39:38Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T16:45:01Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2018-07-20T21:42:23Z","updated_at":"2018-07-28T20:54:44Z","closed_at":"2018-07-28T20:54:44Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Commit 7ed97b4cabf0751e2904aae0dbf34ef24618ed56 removed the defaulted operator= from vector types and replaced it with a non-default implementation. This causes GCC 8's -Wclass-memaccess (enabled by -Wall) to (rightfully) complain when you try to memcpy anything containing a i.e. a glm::vec3.\r\n\r\nSimple example:\r\n\r\n    #include <glm/glm.hpp>\r\n    #include <cstring>\r\n    \r\n    int main() {\r\n    \tglm::vec3 a = glm::vec3(0);\r\n    \tglm::vec3 b;\r\n    \tstd::memcpy(&b, &a, sizeof(glm::vec3));\r\n    \treturn b[0];\r\n    }\r\n\r\nOutput with -Wall:\r\n\r\n    test.cpp: In function ‘int main()’:\r\n    test.cpp:10:39: warning: ‘void* memcpy(void*, const void*, size_t)’ writing to an object of type ‘glm::vec3’ {aka ‘struct glm::vec<3, float, (glm::qualifier)0>’} with no trivial copy-assignment; use copy-assignment or copy-initialization instead [-Wclass-memaccess]\r\n      std::memcpy(&b, &a, sizeof(glm::vec3));\r\n                                           ^\r\n    In file included from /home/dscharrer/pro/build/deps/glm-git/glm/vec3.hpp:8,\r\n                     from /home/dscharrer/pro/build/deps/glm-git/glm/glm.hpp:107,\r\n                     from test.cpp:1:\r\n    /home/dscharrer/pro/build/deps/glm-git/glm/detail/type_vec3.hpp:17:9: note: ‘glm::vec3’ {aka ‘struct glm::vec<3, float, (glm::qualifier)0>’} declared here\r\n      struct vec<3, T, Q>\r\n             ^~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n\r\nWhat was the problem with the previous implementation? It seems to work fine for vectors at least with GCC 4.8 and GCC 8 here.","closed_by":{"login":"Groovounet","id":367227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzIyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://